{title: 323 - O for a Heart to Praise My God!}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #323 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 323}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G/D]O [Am/C]for [Bm]a [G]heart to praise [C/G]my [Em/B]God, [Bm]A [Em/B]heart [G]from [F#dim]sin [Am/C]set [Bm]free,
[G]Aheart that [Bm/F#]always [F#dim]feels [G]Thy blood So [G#m]freely [Am]shed [D7/C]for [Em/B]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G/D]A [Bm]heart [G]resigned, [Em/B]submissive, [Am/C]meek,
[G/D]My dear Redeemer's [Am/C]throne,
[G]Where only Christ is heard [Am]to [D7/C]speak,
[G]Where Jesus reigns [G#m]alone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G/D]A [Bm]heart [G]in every thought [F#dim]renewed
[G/D]And full of [Em/B]love [G]divine,
[G]Perfect [Bm/F#]and [G]right and pure [Am]and [D7/C]good,
[G]A copy, Lord, [G#m]of [D7/C]Thine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G/D]Thy [Bm]nature, [G/D]gracious [Em/B]Lord, [Am/E]impart;
[G/D]Come quickly [Em/B]from [G]above;
[G]Write Thy [Bm/F#]new [G]name upon [Am]my [D7/C]heart,
[G]Thy new, [F#dim]best [G]name [G#m]of [D7/C]Love.
{end_of_verse}
